# Build-context filter for examples/espnet/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit gives a Dockerfile-specific ignore-file precedence over the
# repo-root .dockerignore, and it REPLACES it rather than merging, so the
# upstream patterns are repeated here verbatim below the .git entry.
#
# .git is excluded on top of the upstream set: it is 270+ MB of the build
# context and nothing in the build reads it. setup.py's only git consumer
# is get_base_commit_in_main_branch(), which returns before any git call
# when VLLM_DOCKER_BUILD_CONTEXT=1 and is not reached at all once
# VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_LOCATION pins the wheel; the package version
# comes from SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION.
.git

# ── Below: copied from the repo-root .dockerignore ────────────────────────
/.venv
/build
/artifacts/vllm-rocm-install/
/bake-config-build-*.json
/wheel-export/
dist
vllm/*.so
vllm/vllm-rs

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

.mypy_cache

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
/build/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeUserPresets.json
develop-eggs/
/dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
rust/target/
